f table fields                         EXTNO   =                    3                                                  TTYPE1  = 'BITVALUE'                                                            TFORM1  = 'J       '                                                            TTYPE2  = 'TELESCOPE'                                                           TFORM2  = '5A      '                                                            TTYPE3  = 'INSTRUMENT'                                                          TFORM3  = '18A     '                                                            TTYPE4  = 'GRATING '                                                            TFORM4  = '6A      '                                                            TTYPE5  = 'HLSP_FILE'                                                           TFORM5  = '70A     '                                                            EXTNAME = 'INSTLGND'           / extension name                                 COMMENT This extension is a legend for the integer identifiers in the instrumentCOMMENT  column of the spectrum extension. Instruments are identified by bitwiseCOMMENT  flags so that any combination of instruments contributing to the data wCOMMENT ithin a spectral element can be identified together. For example, if insCOMMENT truments 4 and 16 (100 and 10000 in binary) both contribute to the data COMMENT in a bin, then that bin will have the value 20, or 10100 in binary, to sCOMMENT ignify that both instruments 4 and 16 have contributed. This is identicaCOMMENT l to the handling of bitwise data quality flags.                        COMMENT Not all of these instruments were used to acquire data for this particulCOMMENT ar spectrum. Therefore, not all the listed HLSP files will exist in the COMMENT database. Also note that polynomial fits for filling spectral gaps were COMMENT not saved as separate spectra.                                          END                                      